        "\n",
        "**Relationship with lstat (right plot)**\n",
        "- Clear negative relationship. As the proportion of lower-status population increases, median house value falls. This is as expected.\n",
        "- The relationship is **nonlinear**: the decline is steep at low `lstat` values and flattens out at higher values, suggesting a log or square root transformation of `lstat` (or a polynomial term) would improve the linear model fit.\n",
        "- Several observations are clustered at `medv = 50`, again reflecting the grouping.\n",
        "\n",
        "Both anomalies (the ceiling at 50 and the nonlinearity) require further investigation, which we cover in Lesson 4 (Diagnostics)."
